Our ferry crews use this board to see open maintenance tickets on the boats. It's been fine for the pilot but it rolls out to the whole fleet Monday and I want it to feel finished. Can you go through it and make it ready? Return the full file as one self-contained HTML page: inline CSS, system fonts, no external assets, and keep the sample data inside it.

```html
<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="utf-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
<title>Open tickets</title>
<style>
  body { font-family: system-ui, sans-serif; background: #ffffff; color: #1d2a33; margin: 0; padding: 16px; }
  h1 { font-size: 20px; }
  table { border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%; }
  th, td { text-align: left; padding: 8px; border-bottom: 1px solid #dde3e8; font-size: 14px; }
  th { background: #eef3f6; }
  .sev-high { color: #c0392b; font-weight: 600; }
  .sev-low { color: #7a8a96; }
  a { color: #2a6fb0; }
</style>
</head>
<body>
<h1>Open tickets</h1>
<table>
  <thead><tr><th>Vessel</th><th>Issue</th><th>Severity</th><th>Reported</th><th></th></tr></thead>
  <tbody id="rows"></tbody>
</table>
<script>
  var tickets = [
    { vessel: 'MV Corrigan', issue: 'Starboard bilge pump cycles on and off every few minutes even with the bilge dry, crew suspect a float switch', sev: 'high', date: '2025-03-02' },
    { vessel: 'MV Aldous Reach', issue: 'Cabin heater thermostat reads 4 degrees low', sev: 'low', date: '2025-03-04' },
    { vessel: 'MV Pennywhistle', issue: 'Gangway lamp out', sev: 'low', date: '2025-03-05' }
  ];
  var rows = document.getElementById('rows');
  tickets.forEach(function (t) {
    var tr = document.createElement('tr');
    tr.innerHTML = '<td>' + t.vessel + '</td><td>' + t.issue + '</td><td class="sev-' + t.sev + '">' + t.sev + '</td><td>' + t.date + '</td><td><a href="#">open</a></td>';
    rows.appendChild(tr);
  });
</script>
</body>
</html>
```

